spes: SPES_M2V_HOST_LINEAR=1 takes a host-allocation linear image although Turnip asks a dedicated allocation of it.

Runtime message (backboardd, 2026-11-15): "a 2D BGRA8Unorm texture of 64x64 over a buffer ... the buffer is a no-copy
buffer, and the device makes no linear image of the texture: it asks a dedicated allocation of a linear image of
VK_FORMAT_B8G8R8A8_UNORM for host allocations ... its texels are copied into an image before each use and back after
each write". Turnip sets requiresDedicatedAllocation for any image with external handle types. Off by default.

--- a/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/texture.rs
+++ b/crates/metal2vulkan-runtime/src/texture.rs
@@ -2712,7 +2712,13 @@
             unsafe { raw_device.get_image_memory_requirements2(&query, &mut requirements) };
             requirements.memory_requirements
         };
-        if dedicated.requires_dedicated_allocation != vk::FALSE {
+        // spes: Turnip answers requiresDedicatedAllocation for every image made with an external
+        // memory handle type (tu_image.cc: `shareable`), host allocations included, though binding
+        // one at an offset of an imported host range is what tu_BindImageMemory2 does for any image.
+        // Refusing it made every IOSurface texture over a no-copy buffer a shadow, copied in before
+        // each encoder and back after (2026-11-15: ~150 full-screen copies a second on the A610).
+        // SPES_M2V_HOST_LINEAR=1 in the process's environment takes the image all the same.
+        if dedicated.requires_dedicated_allocation != vk::FALSE && !spes_host_linear() {
             // SAFETY: the image is live and unbound, and no command uses it.
             unsafe { release::object(raw_device, raw) };
             return Ok(Err(LinearRefusal::Dedicated));
@@ -5802,3 +5808,10 @@
     /// (`two_planes.rs`).
     planes: bool,
 }
+
+/// spes: whether `SPES_M2V_HOST_LINEAR=1` asks a host-allocation linear image to be taken although
+/// the driver asks a dedicated allocation of it (`host_linear_image`). Read once.
+fn spes_host_linear() -> bool {
+    static ON: std::sync::OnceLock<bool> = std::sync::OnceLock::new();
+    *ON.get_or_init(|| std::env::var_os("SPES_M2V_HOST_LINEAR").is_some_and(|v| v == "1"))
+}
